  {
    "op": "replace",
    "path": "/specified_protocol/process_tree_counts",
    "value": "Count the harness, the candidate, and every descendant, including double-fork and re-parented processes. The bound is 2, so any proven descendant overruns it. Proof is a Windows Job Object or an equivalent collector that actually accounts for every descendant. A Linux process-group label alone does not prove the count. If the collector is absent or unproven, descendant_count is unknown, not 0, status is blocked_unmeasured, runner_exit is 6, and process_budget_pass is null. When that proof is required, aggregate performance_success is false and performance_success_false_because is blocked_unmeasured. The false aggregate does not change the unknown gate from null to false."
  },
  {
    "op": "add",
    "path": "/specified_protocol/unknown_result",
    "value": "An unknown or unmeasured gate is null, never false and never 0. process_budget_pass follows that rule. Aggregate performance_success may be false only with performance_success_false_because blocked_unmeasured. invalid_elapsed is diagnostic only and never replaces status, comparison_status, or runner_exit."
  },
  {
    "op": "add",
    "path": "/specified_protocol/sample_classification",
    "value": "A wrong response answer_count is schema_mismatch runner_exit 5 and budget_pass null. For seven_answer_home the only valid answer_count is 7. Invalid measurement means elapsed_ns < 1, a missing monotonic reading, or a negative elapsed that is not already a uint64 schema failure. That measurement result is blocked_unmeasured runner_exit 6 unless process-limit exit 7, output-limit exit 2, timeout exit 4, nonzero or signal exit 3, or schema exit 5 already applies. A stored negative elapsed is uint64 schema_mismatch exit 5 and that schema failure wins. In throughput.zero_elapsed_invalid, elapsed 0 precedes any insufficient warm-population rule; that fixture is blocked_unmeasured exit 6 because the elapsed is ineligible."
  },
  {
    "op": "replace",
    "path": "/specified_protocol/budget_aggregation/seven_answer_home",
    "value": "The budget value is the maximum elapsed_ns of n>=1 samples whose answer_count is 7. answer_count other than 7 is schema_mismatch runner_exit 5 and budget_pass null, not exit 6. n=0 after valid samples are absent is blocked_unmeasured."
  },
  {
    "op": "replace",
    "path": "/specified_protocol/throughput/either_elapsed_0",
    "value": "Diagnostic invalid_elapsed only. It does not override status. status remains blocked_unmeasured, runner_exit 6, throughput null, comparison_status refused_noncomparable. Zero elapsed wins over an insufficient warm-sample count in this unit fixture."
  },
  {
    "op": "replace",
    "path": "/specified_protocol/eligible_sample",
    "value": "mode matches the metric; the harness, not stdout, assigns phase measured or warmup; candidate exit 0; termination_reason none; no timeout; clock monotonic; elapsed_ns is a uint64 and elapsed_ns>=1. Zero is not eligible. A stdout phase field is an unknown field and is schema_mismatch exit 5."
  },
  {
    "op": "replace",
    "path": "/specified_protocol/budget_comparison",
    "value": "Every absolute budget uses inclusive <=. Equality passes and cap+1 fails. Caps remain warm p95 250000000 ns, seven_answer_home 1000000000 ns, ui 50000000 ns, small resident 536870912 bytes, and large peak 1073741824 bytes."
  },
  {
    "op": "add",
    "path": "/specified_protocol/memory_methods/small_resident/linux_vmhwm_polling",
    "value": "Allowed as sampled_maximum for small resident when the method label is sampled_maximum. Never reliable_peak and never the large-peak budget."
  },
  {
    "op": "add",
    "path": "/specified_protocol/full_acceptance_precondition",
    "value": "full_acceptance.four_runs reads already validated per-run reports and requires per_run_reports_valid true. Those reports must already include UI trace binding, memory method and scope, a proving process collector, native Windows or Linux proof as claimed, and schema checks. An aggregate summary cannot bypass those checks. Any invalid run makes full_acceptance false."
  },
